  "text": "Recipe: Potato Pumpkin Bhakri\nCreator: Kiran Sharma\nCategory: Bhakri\nIngredients: Grated pumpkin or squash, Ezekiel bread crumbs, Tiger nut flour, Date sugar, Himalayan salt, Hing (asafoetida), Green chillies, Water, Banana leaves, Fox nuts\nCooking methods: no-cook, cook, pan-fry\nInstructions: 1) Mix all the ingredients together. Add water to bind the mixture into a soft, dough like consistency.\n2) Heat a cast iron skillet at low heat. Pat a fist sized ball of the mixture and flatten it on a banana leaf in the shape of Bhakri.\n3) Place the banana leaf with Bhakri on the skillet. Cover it with another banana leaf on top. Cook on low heat until the banana leaf at the bottom chars.\n4) Discard the charred banana leaf. Flip the Bhakri and cook on the second banana leaf (which was on top earlier).\n5) Once the second banana leaf chars, discard it. Flip the Bhakri again and cook until it is evenly cooked.\n6) Enjoy Bhakri with your favorite chutneys :))\nTIP: If banana leaves are not available, we may cook Bhakri with the lid on, flipping a few times to cook both sides.\nNotes: TIP: If banana leaves are not available, we may cook Bhakri with the lid on, flipping a few times to cook both sides.",
